        context_item("Activity 1 — Activity Synthesis", "• Reread the story about 6 children listening to a story.\n• “What did we do first to act out this story?” (First, 6 of\nus acted like we were listening.)\n• “What did we do next to act out this story?” (Then 4\nmore people came and pretended to listen.)\n• “How did you know that 4 people should join the\ngroup?” (Because in the story, 4 more kids joined.)\n• “The words in a story help us figure out what is\nhappening. If you imagine what is happening in the\nstory, it can help us solve the problem.“", line(220)),
        context_item("Activity 2 — Activity Synthesis", "• Invite previously selected students to share for each\nproblem.\n• “What are the different ways we represented what\nhappened in each story?”\n• As needed, “we can also represent each story with an\nexpression. I know the first story matches 5 and 2\nmore or 5 + 2.”\n• “How could we represent the second story with an\nexpression?” (It matches 5 take away 2, so 5 - 2.)", line(322)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "“Today we read story problems and represented them in different ways.”\n\nDisplay and read “A group of kids was using 10 puppets to act out a story. They put 5 of the puppets away. How many\npuppets do they have now?”\n\n“Tell your partner what happened in the story.”\n\n“What are ways we could show what is happening in this problem?” (Act it out, draw pictures, write “10 take away 5”,\n10- 5 )\n\nRecord student responses on chart paper for reference in future lessons.", line(343))
