    [
        context_item("Warm-up — Activity Synthesis", "• “How can you use the result of 14- 6 to find the\nvalue of 54- 6 ?” (54 has 4 more tens than 14, so add\n4 tens or 40 to the result of 14- 6 .)\n• “How can you use the result of 54- 6 to find the\nvalue of 54- 26 ?” (26 has 2 more tens than 6, so that\nmeans 2 tens need to be taken away from the result\nof54- 6 .)", line(110)),
        context_item("Activity 1 — Activity Synthesis", "• Invite previously selected students to share the\ncategories for their sorts.\n• Record the various categories.\n• “What do you notice about the different ways we\nsorted the cards? How are they the same? How are\nthey different?” (There are some categories that are\nabout how many steps it takes to solve the problem.\nSome categories are about what’s going on in the\nproblem, like if it is comparing or not. Some\ncategories are about whether the story is about\naddition or subtraction. Some people used addition\nand subtraction as categories, but used different\n\ncards.)\n• If students do not sort in any of the ways suggested\nin the Student Responses, propose these categories\nand ask students to use them to sort.", line(219)),
        context_item("Activity 2 — Activity Synthesis", "• Invite selected students to share their solutions for\nthe story with Jada’s books in stacks of 10.\n• “How are their methods the same? How are they\ndifferent?”", line(299)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "Read the story problem about the books in Elena’s class.\n\nDraw a diagram to show:\n\n“How does the diagram represent the problem?” (It shows a part of the tape diagram for each day they sorted books. It\nshows the unknown is the total number of books they sorted.)\n\n“How does the diagram help you see how to solve the problem?” (It shows me I need to add 47, 15, and 18. I know I can\nadd the numbers in any order.)\n\n“What are other ways you or others made sense of story problems that had more than one step?”", line(321))
    ],
    source('curriculum/im_teacher_guides/grade2/unit9/lesson9.md')).

