        context_item("Activity 1 — Student Task Statement", "1. Jada has 4 times as many cubes as Kiran. Draw\na diagram to represent the situation.\n2. Diego has 5 times as many cubes as Kiran.\nDraw a diagram to represent the situation.\n3. Lin has 6 times as many cubes as Kiran. How\nmany cubes does Lin have? Explain or show\nyour reasoning.", line(153)),
        context_item("Activity 2 — Student Task Statement", "Here are 4 sets of descriptions, diagrams, and\nequations that compare pairs of quantities.\nMatch each description to a diagram and an\nequation that represent the same situation.\n\nA                          B\nLin has 3 cubes.           Han has 3 cubes.\n\nJada has 2 times as        Elena has 3 times as\nmany.                      many.\n\nD\nC\nPriya had 5 cubes.\n2 × 3 = 6              Noah had 3 times as\nmany.\n\nE                          F\n\n3 × 5 = 15                 4 × 4 = 16\n\nG                          H\n\nJ\nI\nMai has 4 cubes.\n3 × 3 = 9              Diego has 4 times as\nmany.\n\nK                          L\n\nRecord your matches here:\n\nSet 1: _____, _____, _____\n\nSet 2: _____, _____, _____\n\nSet 3: _____, _____, _____\n\nSet 4: _____, _____, _____", line(251)),
        context_item("Cool-down — Student Task Statement", "1. Circle the statement and the multiplication equation that show a comparison of Tyler’s and Elena’s cubes.\n\nTyler has 4 more cubes than Elena.                                           6 × 4 = 24\n\nElena has 5 times as many cubes as Tyler.                                    2 × 10 = 20\n\nTyler has 5 times as many cubes as Elena.                                    4 × 4 = 16\n\nTyler has 4 times as many cubes as Elena.                                    5 × 4 = 20\n\n2. Explain your choices.", line(369))
