    [
        context_item("Warm-up — Activity Synthesis", "• “Is 105 a multiple of 2, 3, or 5? How do you know?” (3\nand 5. I know 90 is a multiple of 2, 3, and 5 so I can\nuse the recorded counts to identify multiples. 105 is\n\nin the recorded counts for 3 and 5.)\n• “Is 105 a multiple of 15?” (Yes. I can count by 15s to\nget to 90: 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90 and then 15 more is\n105.)", line(119)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "“Today we solved problems that involved division with and without remainders. What strategies did you find yourself\nusing to divide numbers? Did you:\n\n• use partial products?\n• use partial quotients?\n• draw diagrams?\n• divide by place value (thousands, hundreds, tens, and ones)?\n• write a series of equations?\n• estimate first?”\n\n“How do we know that there will be reminders when we divide?” (We know when the dividend is less than the divisor\nthat we do not have enough to make another group or to put an equal amount in each group.)\n\n“What if the remainder was four flowers left over after all the flower pots were filled, what would we do then?” (We could\nput more flowers in some pots or just give the extra flowers away.)", line(298))
