        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "“Today we learned how to represent the multiplication of 2 two-digit numbers using a rectangular diagram. We learned\nthat we can decompose each factor by place value and show the tens and ones on each side of the rectangle, and that\ndoing this can help us to multiply efficiently.”\n\nSelect students with different strategies to share their reasoning for finding the value of         (the last problem of the\nlast activity).\n\nDisplay the following diagram as an example of how decomposing can result in\nfacts that are not helpful when multiplying to support using place value to\ndecompose.\n\n“Why might it be more helpful to decompose 55 into            than into          ?” (Multiplying by multiples of 10 and by\n\nsingle-digit numbers is easier than multiplying numbers like 42 and 9.)", line(309))
