        context_item("Activity 1 — Activity Synthesis", "MLR3 Critique, Correct, Clarify\n• Display Elena’s partially correct answer and\nexplanation for students to consider.\n• Read the explanation aloud.\n\n• “What parts of this response are unclear, incorrect,\nor incomplete?” (She says the answer will be more\nthan 621, but she doesn’t say how much more. The\nanswer will be a lot more than 628.68.)\n• 1 minute: quiet think time\n• 2 minute: partner discussion\n• Invite 2–3 groups share what they discussed. Record\nfor all to see.\n• “With your partner, work together to write a revised\nsolution and explanation.”\n• Display and review the following criteria:\n\n◦ Explain each step.\n◦ Use “decimal point,” “tenths,” “hundredths,” or\nother place value words.\n◦ Label your work with details that help your\nexplanation.\n• 3–5 minutes: partner work time\n• Select 1–2 groups to read their revised draft aloud\nslowly enough to record for all to see. Scribe as each\ngroup shares. Then invite the whole class to\ncontribute additional language and edits to make the\nfinal draft even more clear and more convincing.\n• “What is the same and different about the revised\nsolutions and explanations?”", line(166)),
        context_item("Activity 2 — Activity Synthesis", "• Invite previously selected students to share.\n• Display: 463 + 3.14\n• “How do you add these using the standard\nalgorithm?” (I made sure that the 3 in 463 lines up\nwith the 3 in 3.14 so I am adding numbers with the\nsame place value. I added 0’s in the tenths and\nhundredths places of 463 to help add the numbers.)\n\n• “Did anyone use a different strategy to add these\nnumbers?” (I knew that 463 and 3 is 466. Then I also\nhave 14 hundredths so it's 466.14.)", line(247)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "“Today we analyzed errors in strategies for adding decimals.”\n\n“Describe what is the most important thing to remember when we add decimal numbers.” (Pay attention to the place\nvalues of the digits that I add together.)\n\n“What are some mistakes someone can make when finding the sum?” (Adding different place value positions. Making an\nerror in writing the expression vertically by not lining up the decimal. Forgetting to write down newly composed units.)", line(272))
