        context_item("Warm-up — Activity Synthesis", "• “If we continue counting, what numbers will be in\n\nboth counts?” (All of the numbers on the second list,\n\nthe ones where we count by 12)\n\n• “Why do you think that happens?” (Each of the\nnumbers in the second list are double the number in\nthe first, so they’ll still be counted when you count by\n6. 12 is       , so 6 is a factor in all the numbers in\nboth lists.)", line(115)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "“Today we generated patterns and recognized relationships between two different patterns.”\n\nDisplay or rewrite the numbers from the 2 Choral Counts in the Warm-up.\n\n“What relationships do you notice between the patterns in the counts?” (Each number in the second count is twice the\nmatching number in the first count. Each number in the first count is one half the matching number in the second\ncount. All the numbers on the second list are also on the first list. The second list is every other number of the first list.)\n\n“Explain to your partner why these relationships will continue if the patterns continue.” (The second pattern adds 12\neach time and that's twice what the first pattern adds each time.)", line(347))
