        context_item("Student Task Statement", "What do you notice? What do you wonder?\n\nTuesday\n\n\n\n\n- Instructional Routines\n- Notice and Wonder\n- 5 min", line(116)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "One batch of a soup recipe uses 9 cups of milk. A chef makes different amounts of soup on different days. Here are the amounts of milk she used:\n\n- Monday: 12 cups\n- Tuesday: cups\n\nFor each question:\n\n- A. Write a multiplication equation and a division equation that represent it. Use the '?' symbol for the unknown value.\n- B. Answer the question. Use the partially started tape diagram to show your reasoning. The shaded region represents the cups of milk in 1 batch.\n1. How many batches of soup did she make on Monday?\n- a. Multiplication equation:\n- b. Answer:\n- Thursday: 6 cups\n- Friday: cups\n- MLR6: Three Reads\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDivision equation:\n\n\n\n\n4\n\n\n\n2. How many batches of soup did she make on Tuesday?\n- a. Multiplication equation: Division equation:\n- b. Answer:\n3. What fraction of a batch of soup did she make on Thursday?\n- a. Multiplication equation:\n- b. Answer:\n4. What fraction of a batch of soup did she make on Friday?\n- a. Multiplication equation: Division equation:\n- b. Answer:", line(244)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "Here is a diagram that shows four ropes of different lengths.\n\n\n\nComplete each sentence comparing the ropes' lengths. Then write a multiplication equation and a division equation for each comparison.\n\n| statement   | statement                | multiplication equation   | division equation   |\n|-------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|---------------------|\n| Rope B is   | times as long as Rope A. |                           |                     |\n| Rope C is   | times as long as Rope A. |                           |                     |\n| Rope D is   | times as long as Rope A. |                           |                     |\n| Rope D is   | times as long as Rope C. |                           |                     |", line(510)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "For each question, write a multiplication equation and a division equation. Then answer the question. You can draw a tape diagram if you find it helpful.\n\n1. What fraction of 9 is 3?\n- a. Multiplication equation:\n- b. Answer:\n2. What fraction of 5 is ?\n- a. Multiplication equation:\n- b. Answer:", line(614)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "There are 6 gallons of water in a 20-gallon fish tank. What fraction of the tank is filled?\n\n1. Write a multiplication equation and a division equation to represent the situation.\n2. Answer the question. You can draw a tape diagram if you find it helpful.", line(755))
