    [
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "What do you notice? What do you wonder?\n\n$$2 t + 5 = 2 t + 5$$", line(105)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "$$n & = n \\\\ & 2 t + 6 = 2 ( t + 3 ) \\\\ 3 ( n + 1 ) & = 3 n + 1 \\\\ \\frac { 1 } { 4 } ( 2 0 d + 4 ) & = 5 d \\\\ \\text {Sort these equations into the two types: true for all values and true for no values}$$\n\n1. Sort these equations into the two types: true for all values and true for no values.\n2. Write the other side of this equation so that this equation is true for all values of .\n\n$$6 ( u - 2 ) + 2 =$$\n\n3. Write the other side of this equation so that this equation is true for no values of .\n\n$$6 ( u - 2 ) + 2 =$$", line(185)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "1. Complete each equation so that it is true for all values of .\n2. a.\n\n$$b . \\ x - 2 = - ( \\underbrace { - x } )$$\n\n$$\\mathbb { c } . \\ \\frac { 1 5 x - 1 0 } { 5 } = \\cfrac { } { } - 2$$\n\n$$b . \\\\ c .$$\n\n2. Complete each equation so that it is true for no values of .\n\n$$a .$$\n\n$$b . \\\\ c .$$\n\n$$\\mathbb { c } . \\ \\frac { 1 5 x - 1 0 } { 5 } = \\cfrac { } { } - 2$$\n\n3. Describe how you know whether an equation will be true for all values of or true for no values of .", line(301)),
        context_item("Student Task Statement", "What value could you write in after \" + \" that would make the equation true for:\n\n1. no values of ?\n2. all values of ?\n3. just one value of ?", line(412))
