        context_item("Activity 2 — Activity Synthesis", "• Invite previously selected students to share in order\nfrom the most common approach to the least\ncommon approach. Record or display their work for\nall to see.\n• Connect students’ approaches by asking:\n◦ “What is the same about the ways they figured\nout how many hexagons were in the circle?”\n(They counted all of the hexagons and got 19\nhexagons.)\n◦ “What is different about the ways they figured\nout how many hexagons were in the circle?”\n(They kept track of the shapes they counted in\ndifferent ways. The first person colored in all the\nhexagons. The next person put cubes on the\nhexagons as they counted them. The last person\nmarked the hexagon they started with and\n\ncounted the rest with their finger.)\n• Connect students’ approaches to the learning goal by\nasking:\n◦ “How does crossing out each shape help you\nkeep track of the shapes you have counted?”\n(When all of the shapes are crossed out, I know\nthat I have counted all of the shapes 1 time.)\n◦ “How does putting a cube on top of each shape\nhelp you keep track of the shapes you have\ncounted?” (I know that I’ve already counted the\nshapes with a cube on top. When all of the\nshapes have a cube on top, I know that I’ve\ncounted all of the shapes 1 time.)\n\n◦ “How does marking the shape you counted first\nhelp you keep track of the shapes you have\ncounted?” (If I know which shape I counted first, I\ncan stop counting right before I touch it again.)\n\n_ trapezoids\n\n_ rectangles", line(313)),
        context_item("Lesson Synthesis", "Display the image from the second activity of 12 triangles in a circle.\n\nDemonstrate counting the triangles incorrectly. Continue counting around the circle even after you’ve counted all of the\ntriangles.\n\n“Did I count correctly? Why or why not?” (You didn’t count correctly because you counted some of the triangles more\nthan 1 time.)\n\nRepeat, but this time demonstrate miscounting the triangles by only counting 11 of them.\n\n“What can I do to make sure that I count each triangle one time and that I don’t forget to count any triangles?” (You can\nput a cube on top of each triangle as you count it. You can cross off each triangle as you count it. You can color each\ntriangle as you count it. You can mark which triangle you counted first.)\n\nKindergarten                                      CC BY NC 2024", line(536))
